IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24-s752`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24a-dangerous-offender`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24b-long-term`

-- ccc28-tests-part24b.l4 -- tests of sections 753.1 to 755. Expected values are written by hand from the words of each provision, on both sides of every threshold.
-- The table of section 753.1(2)(a) is parsed from the line of the source text by work/tables.py (not from the encoding).

§ `Test fixtures (not law)`

GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A STRING
      implication IS A `s 752 how the offender is implicated`
GIVETH A `s 752 offence`
`s 753.1 test the offence` MEANS
    `s 752 offence` OF `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`, (`Provision of the Code` OF section, subsection), implication, (Date 1 1 2020), FALSE

§ `s 753.1(1): the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender`

#ASSERT `s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application following the filing of a report
#ASSERT `s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court is not satisfied of (a): a grant limited by an "if", not covered
#ASSERT `s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court is not satisfied of (b)
#ASSERT `s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court is not satisfied of (c)
#ASSERT `s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

